Add APC tracking (v0.130)

Dan confirmed v0.129's APC booking fix worked end to end and asked for
tracking wired up "the same way as DPD" - i.e. a Track button on the order
screen.

DPD's Track button is just a plain link to DPD's public tracking site
(track.dpd.co.uk), built client-side from the consignment number - no API
call needed. APC has no confirmed equivalent: the closest public tracker
found (APC Choice, apcchoice.apc-overnight.com) asks for a "7-digit
consignment number", which doesn't match the 22-digit Hypaship WayBill
this app stores, so there was no way to be confident a plain link would
actually work.

Used APC's own authenticated Tracks.json endpoint instead (documented in
section 5 of the integration guide): GET
Tracks/{waybill}.json?searchtype=CarrierWaybill&history=Yes, same
remote-user auth as every other APC call. ApcShippingService.trackShipment
walks the response's nested Items/Item/Activity/Status structure (one
Activity array per shipment piece), flattens every scan into a single
list, and sorts it newest-first. A "Track" button on the order screen
calls this through the backend and shows the latest status inline, with
the full scan history tucked under a "Full scan history" toggle so it
doesn't dominate the page for the common case.

